// cppcheck suppressions, applied by tools/quality_check.py.
// One id per line; say why.

// Headers are found through -I for first-party code only; the system's and
// the fetched dependencies' are left unread on purpose (speed).
missingInclude
missingIncludeSystem

// Fires on every aggregate with a std::string or a span member. The members
// that really are indeterminate are reported by clang-tidy
// (cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init).
uninitMemberVarNoCtor

// An unread dependency leaves a macro or a type unknown; that is not a
// finding about this code.
unknownMacro
checkersReport

// A mutex that exists only so a condition variable can be waited on
// (Clock::sleep_for, and the tests of wait_until): nothing else is meant to
// lock it.
localMutex

// `&tokens[i]` then `fields[1]`: a pointer into a vector's elements, which
// cppcheck takes for the address of one object.
objectIndex

// In tests: `ASSERT_TRUE(v.empty()) << v.front()` builds its message only
// when the assertion fails, and QCOMPARE and QVERIFY return when they fail.
// cppcheck sees neither, and reports what follows as reached regardless.
containerOutOfBounds:tests/*
nullPointer:tests/ui/*

// Valid C++ that cppcheck 2.22 cannot parse (a reverse iterator in a for
// statement; pointers to members in an initializer). It checks NOTHING in
// these two files past that line: they are clang-tidy's alone. Try again
// with each new cppcheck and take the line out when it parses.
syntaxError:libs/experiment/src/model/experiment_queue.cpp
syntaxError:libs/ingest/src/writer.cpp
